* ============================================================================
* 03_04_sqlite_capability_gap_v2.dts
*
* Replaces 03_dbf_to_sqlite_students.dts and 04_sqlite_select_to_dbf_people.dts.
*
* THESE TWO TESTS WERE NOT REPAIRED. They asked the engine to do things it does
* not implement, and rewriting them into something that passes would have hidden
* a real roadmap gap behind a green result. This script instead proves exactly
* what the SQLite surface CAN do, and states precisely where it stops.
*
* WHY 03 COULD NOT RUN
*   BEGIN                 -- not a registered command (0 hits, shell_commands.cpp)
*   SCAN + #SID, #LNAME.. -- no field-substitution implementation exists, so the
*                            SQL string is never populated from cursor values
*   The intent -- pump DBF rows into SQLite -- has no expressible form today.
*
* WHY 04 COULD NOT RUN
*   SQLITE QUERY "..." INTO DBF <file>
*                         -- SQLITE has no QUERY subcommand (0 hits) and no
*                            INTO-DBF materialisation path. SQLITE SELECT prints
*                            a capped result set to the console; it cannot write
*                            a file that AUTODBF could then consume.
*
* Both originals also wrote to _drops/, which does not exist.
* ============================================================================

SET TALK ON
ECHO CONVGAP BEGIN sqlite-surface

* -- what DOES work: connect, DDL, literal DML, read back -----------------------
ECHO CONVGAP PROVEN connect-ddl-dml-select
SQLITE DB tmp/conv_gap_probe.sqlite
SQLITE STATUS
SQLITE EXEC DROP TABLE IF EXISTS conversion_gap_probe
SQLITE EXEC CREATE TABLE conversion_gap_probe (sku TEXT, std_cost REAL, active INTEGER)
SQLITE EXEC INSERT INTO conversion_gap_probe VALUES ('RAW-SHAFT-4140', 48.0, 1)
SQLITE EXEC INSERT INTO conversion_gap_probe VALUES ('RAW-HOUS-AL', 62.0, 1)
SQLITE TABLES
SQLITE COLUMNS conversion_gap_probe
SQLITE SELECT SELECT COUNT(*) AS N FROM conversion_gap_probe
SQLITE SELECT SELECT sku, std_cost, active FROM conversion_gap_probe ORDER BY sku
SQLITE CLOSE

* -- the two gaps, asserted as gaps --------------------------------------------
ECHO CONVGAP GAP1 dbf-to-sqlite-row-pump NOT-IMPLEMENTED
ECHO CONVGAP GAP1 needs field substitution in SCAN/SQLITE EXEC or a bulk command
ECHO CONVGAP GAP2 sqlite-result-to-file NOT-IMPLEMENTED
ECHO CONVGAP GAP2 needs SQLITE result set written to CSV or DBF for AUTODBF pickup

ECHO CONVGAP END

* ============================================================================
* PASS CRITERIA
*   SQLITE STATUS reports a connection to tmp/conv_gap_probe.sqlite
*   SQLITE TABLES lists conversion_gap_probe
*   SQLITE COLUMNS reports 3 columns: sku TEXT, std_cost REAL, active INTEGER
*   COUNT query returns 2
*   the ORDER BY select prints both rows, RAW-HOUS-AL first
*
* This proves the SQLite surface is live and usable for DDL, literal DML and
* queries. It does NOT prove any DBF <-> SQLite data movement, because no such
* path exists.
*
* CONSEQUENCE FOR THE PDLC CHAIN
*   The chartered chain is:
*     fixed-record COBOL -> DBF -> CSV/JSON -> SQLite -> x64base
*   The SQLite legs are currently untraversable from inside DotTalk++ in either
*   direction. CSV -> x64base is proven (10_crosswalk_cascade_items_v1.dts).
*   DBF -> CSV is repaired and pending a recorded run (01, 05 v2).
*   Closing GAP1 and GAP2 is what would make the full chain demonstrable.
* ============================================================================
